WEBVTT

01:33.343 --> 01:37.847
DELICIOUS IN DUNGEON

01:43.812 --> 01:44.938
I'm so tired.

01:45.021 --> 01:46.189
All these stairs...

01:46.272 --> 01:48.191
doesn't it feel like
you're twice as tired?

01:48.274 --> 01:51.194
A moderate amount of fatigue
makes your meal taste better.

01:51.277 --> 01:52.987
In moderation, sure.

01:55.240 --> 01:56.449
Give me your sword.

01:56.950 --> 01:57.826
Sure.

02:00.578 --> 02:02.956
There should be a trick door around here.

02:14.384 --> 02:17.804
I almost forgot that the door led here.

02:17.887 --> 02:19.764
It saved us quite a bit of time.

02:22.392 --> 02:23.643
Huh?

02:24.144 --> 02:25.353
What is it?

02:26.396 --> 02:28.690
The decoration on my sword guard is gone.

02:29.274 --> 02:31.109
It's because you were reckless with it.

02:31.943 --> 02:33.069
Was it my fault?

02:33.903 --> 02:36.656
No, it was coming loose for a while now.

02:37.782 --> 02:41.661
<i>I was trying to hold it together
with string or glue,</i>

02:41.744 --> 02:42.745
<i>but I guess it was time.</i>

02:43.663 --> 02:45.832
Is there a problem if it's gone?

02:45.915 --> 02:47.458
Nope. Not at all.

02:48.751 --> 02:50.587
Was it a memento or something?

02:50.670 --> 02:53.548
A memento... I suppose you could say that.

02:54.757 --> 02:57.719
<i>Three years ago,
when I was just a beginner,</i>

02:57.802 --> 03:01.180
<i>I joined a gold-peeling crew
to get some experience.</i>

03:01.723 --> 03:03.099
<i>Gold-peeling?</i>

03:03.182 --> 03:06.477
<i>A long time ago, this castle
was completely covered in gold,</i>

03:06.561 --> 03:08.354
<i>and peeling it made quite a profit.</i>

03:10.815 --> 03:13.276
This place has been
mostly peeled already.

03:14.068 --> 03:15.987
Let's see if there's anything
inside the castle.

03:16.070 --> 03:17.155
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

03:17.238 --> 03:21.534
Laios, isn't it dangerous for us to enter
the castle with our current abilities?

03:21.618 --> 03:25.330
Yeah, but the two of us
can't turn back on our own.

03:31.878 --> 03:33.338
What the hell?

03:33.421 --> 03:34.797
How awful.

03:34.881 --> 03:36.758
It's completely rotten away.

03:36.841 --> 03:39.010
I guess that's what happens
if you die in here.

03:39.093 --> 03:40.887
No one finds you.

03:41.638 --> 03:43.765
Hey! Come over here!

03:50.855 --> 03:53.066
You could probably sell these.

03:53.149 --> 03:54.692
They're better than what we saw earlier,

03:54.776 --> 03:57.153
but you can only melt them down
and sell them for ingredients...

03:59.489 --> 04:01.532
T-The armor moved!

04:01.616 --> 04:03.284
It's a monster! Run!

04:04.494 --> 04:06.788
We're no match for it. Run!

04:13.586 --> 04:15.004
You...!

04:18.883 --> 04:20.885
D-Dammit!

04:20.969 --> 04:22.136
My sword...

04:32.647 --> 04:33.481
Come on...!

04:42.073 --> 04:43.574
I did it!

04:44.200 --> 04:45.994
- Laios!
- Huh?

04:50.039 --> 04:52.500
<i>Something like that happened.</i>

04:53.251 --> 04:55.086
And this is the sword I got then.

04:55.169 --> 04:56.379
So you lost...

04:56.462 --> 05:00.967
It was my first death, so for a while,
simply seeing an armor terrified me.

05:02.468 --> 05:06.681
I read a lot of documents,
but none of them described how they taste.

05:07.223 --> 05:09.350
I wonder what they taste like.

05:10.226 --> 05:12.395
Senshi, how would you cook them?

05:13.604 --> 05:15.523
Armor isn't edible.

05:15.606 --> 05:20.028
Living Armor is simply controlled
by magic, and it's not some creature.

05:20.111 --> 05:21.988
I-I know that, but...

05:22.071 --> 05:23.990
What about the leather clasps?

05:24.073 --> 05:26.451
It's difficult to eat tanned hide,

05:27.160 --> 05:30.288
and it's far easier
to catch other monsters.

05:30.872 --> 05:34.042
If you're that hungry for armor,
cook and eat your own.

05:36.169 --> 05:37.128
I see.

05:37.211 --> 05:39.672
I guess we can't eat Living Armor.

05:41.090 --> 05:42.300
Come on, let's go.

05:45.887 --> 05:48.014
I'd rather not fight them now.

05:48.514 --> 05:50.016
How about running our way past them?

05:50.641 --> 05:54.020
They're slow,
so we could easily shake them off.

05:54.103 --> 05:55.229
True.

05:56.481 --> 05:58.274
Are you all okay with that?

05:58.357 --> 05:59.400
Sure.

06:00.026 --> 06:01.903
We don't know
which set of armor might move.

06:01.986 --> 06:03.404
Everyone, be careful.

06:03.488 --> 06:04.405
Ready?

06:18.127 --> 06:19.462
H-Here comes!

06:27.053 --> 06:28.096
Run!

06:56.040 --> 06:59.210
Our way is completely blocked!

06:59.293 --> 07:00.711
What the heck?

07:00.795 --> 07:03.589
H-Hey! This is bad!

07:03.673 --> 07:05.967
Let's turn back for now and regroup!

07:06.551 --> 07:08.094
Pull back!

07:17.478 --> 07:19.772
They're especially persistent today.

07:19.856 --> 07:22.150
I wonder if something
put them in a bad mood.

07:22.233 --> 07:23.109
No way!

07:23.693 --> 07:26.446
They don't have
physical conditions or feelings.

07:26.988 --> 07:30.867
That's why it should be easy if we can
defeat whoever is controlling them.

07:30.950 --> 07:33.244
Are you sure there's someone?

07:33.327 --> 07:34.495
I've never seen them.

07:35.580 --> 07:37.248
USUALLY

07:37.331 --> 07:40.710
<i>Usually, they only attack anyone
who gets close to them.</i>

07:41.252 --> 07:44.505
<i>But today, they clearly blocked our path.</i>

07:45.339 --> 07:50.303
<i>In other words, maybe they're
guarding something that's farther ahead.</i>

07:51.471 --> 07:53.973
Whoever is controlling them is close by?

07:54.682 --> 07:57.143
You're right. That might be possible.

07:57.226 --> 07:59.937
What? Is it a monster?

08:00.021 --> 08:01.189
I don't know.

08:01.272 --> 08:04.817
But a magic-user with such power
can't be anyone decent!

08:05.818 --> 08:09.739
Anyway, we have to find a way
to get past that barrier of armor and...

08:10.239 --> 08:13.826
So, if we can reach the magic-user
who is controlling the Living Armor,

08:13.910 --> 08:16.746
we might be able to stop them.

08:16.829 --> 08:18.289
But how?

08:18.372 --> 08:19.415
For example...

08:19.999 --> 08:22.126
Three of us act as bait
to draw their attention

08:22.210 --> 08:24.504
while one of us goes past the door.

08:28.257 --> 08:29.592
Good luck.

08:30.760 --> 08:32.803
I thought you might be
the most fitting for the role

08:32.887 --> 08:34.931
since you're good at going unnoticed.

08:35.014 --> 08:36.933
I'm no good in combat.

08:37.600 --> 08:40.269
Besides, Living Armor
doesn't have eyes or ears,

08:40.353 --> 08:43.272
so going unnoticed doesn't help much
against something that's not alive.

08:44.357 --> 08:46.025
Doesn't have eyes or ears...

08:52.031 --> 08:53.074
Are you ready?

08:53.908 --> 08:56.327
All right! Let's go!

08:56.911 --> 08:57.828
Come on!

08:57.912 --> 09:01.207
Gather around us, you sets of armor!

09:02.250 --> 09:03.417
They're all coming!

09:03.501 --> 09:04.710
Don't panic!

09:15.012 --> 09:15.846
<i>Aslam!</i>

09:42.582 --> 09:44.875
What? There's another Living Armor here?

09:49.422 --> 09:52.300
<i>I've never seen this type of armor move.</i>

09:53.259 --> 09:55.928
<i>I don't see anyone
who's controlling it, though.</i>

09:56.470 --> 09:58.931
<i>It looks stronger
than the armor back there.</i>

10:01.934 --> 10:04.145
<i>I can't call for backup, though.</i>

10:04.228 --> 10:08.482
<i>Anyway, I have to figure out on my own
what they're guarding.</i>

10:14.739 --> 10:16.490
<i>I'll cut off its arm or leg</i>

10:16.574 --> 10:18.492
<i>and render it immobile!</i>

10:41.015 --> 10:42.725
Dammit! You...!

10:52.193 --> 10:54.278
<i>Why did it guard its shield?</i>

10:55.404 --> 10:56.489
<i>What's that?</i>

10:59.033 --> 11:00.743
<i>There's something on its shield.</i>

11:01.369 --> 11:04.747
<i>Somehow, it seems very familiar.</i>

11:11.754 --> 11:12.755
<i>Right.</i>

11:16.801 --> 11:17.885
<i>It's...</i>

11:23.974 --> 11:25.142
<i>An egg case!</i>

11:25.768 --> 11:27.853
<i>It's an egg of some creature.</i>

11:27.937 --> 11:28.896
<i>That's what it shielded!</i>

11:32.149 --> 11:34.068
<i>But what egg could it be?</i>

11:34.568 --> 11:36.737
<i>Is it the egg of whoever
is controlling the armor?</i>

11:36.821 --> 11:40.116
<i>Besides, Living Armor
doesn't have eyes or ears.</i>

11:40.199 --> 11:41.325
<i>That's not it!</i>

11:41.409 --> 11:42.910
<i>It's been bugging me all this time.</i>

11:43.702 --> 11:45.496
<i>They're inorganic, without eyes or ears.</i>

11:46.455 --> 11:48.749
<i>The way they pick up their head
and put it back on.</i>

11:49.625 --> 11:52.336
<i>The way they turn their head
and follow our movements.</i>

11:53.337 --> 11:54.839
<i>And the egg...</i>

11:56.090 --> 11:58.717
<i>There's no doubt about it!
They're living creatures!</i>

11:59.885 --> 12:01.679
<i>No one is giving them orders.</i>

12:02.346 --> 12:06.559
<i>They're simply acting on their instincts
and trying to protect the egg.</i>

12:07.476 --> 12:10.646
<i>In that case,
there are many ways to defeat them!</i>

12:12.106 --> 12:12.940
<i>And...</i>

12:14.608 --> 12:15.568
<i>they're edible!</i>

12:22.783 --> 12:24.034
This is endless!

12:25.035 --> 12:26.287
Are you serious?!

12:28.998 --> 12:31.083
Don't pause! It's dangerous if you freeze!

12:31.167 --> 12:32.418
Senshi! Behind you!

12:33.252 --> 12:34.295
<i>Aslam!</i>

12:35.379 --> 12:37.756
Huh? Hey!

12:42.887 --> 12:44.263
Do they share parts?

12:44.346 --> 12:45.181
What?!

12:45.264 --> 12:46.807
Is that even possible?!

12:48.601 --> 12:49.935
Hey, Laios!

12:50.019 --> 12:52.771
Do something about these armors quickly!

12:54.273 --> 12:57.276
<i>These Living Armors don't die
even when you cut off their heads.</i>

12:57.359 --> 12:59.945
<i>But if they're creatures,
they must be killable.</i>

13:00.029 --> 13:05.451
<i>Either by internal injury, outflow
of body fluid, suffocation, or starvation.</i>

13:06.035 --> 13:08.370
<i>It's not realistic to try a method
that takes time.</i>

13:08.454 --> 13:12.291
<i>First, I need to determine
the form of the creature that is inside.</i>

13:14.418 --> 13:18.839
<i>For an amorphous creature like a Slime,
its movements are too rigid.</i>

13:20.925 --> 13:23.219
<i>Is it possible that they're swarms
of tiny creatures?</i>

13:23.302 --> 13:25.638
<i>But they don't make any sound,
so that seems unlikely.</i>

13:26.263 --> 13:29.975
<i>Or maybe creatures with long limbs
are controlling them from inside.</i>

13:31.018 --> 13:32.895
<i>They could be other creatures,</i>

13:34.063 --> 13:36.398
<i>but it's probably easier
to see for myself.</i>

13:37.107 --> 13:39.026
<i>It doesn't seem like
I can match it in strength.</i>

13:39.860 --> 13:40.736
<i>In that case,</i>

13:41.320 --> 13:42.738
<i>I only have one option!</i>

13:42.821 --> 13:45.783
<i>Go for the shield with the egg attached,
and make it drop its guard!</i>

13:57.086 --> 13:58.254
Got it!

14:00.381 --> 14:01.882
What's inside? Huh?

14:02.716 --> 14:04.134
There's nothing!

14:06.220 --> 14:07.721
It's empty.

14:08.264 --> 14:11.141
Could it have been a camouflage tactic
when it retrieved its head?

14:12.560 --> 14:13.644
<i>This is bad.</i>

14:13.727 --> 14:15.896
I need... I need to think of my next move!

14:19.650 --> 14:20.526
What?

14:21.443 --> 14:24.405
<i>Couldn't it see which pillar I hid behind?</i>

14:25.531 --> 14:27.241
<i>There must be something in its head, then.</i>

14:28.617 --> 14:29.618
A gap?

14:39.628 --> 14:42.590
I see. It was a mollusk!

14:42.673 --> 14:44.800
It was clinging to the inside.

14:45.467 --> 14:47.136
<i>Could it have survived amputation</i>

14:47.219 --> 14:49.680
<i>because it was a colony
of many creatures to begin with?</i>

14:50.723 --> 14:52.433
<i>Is it looking for its head?</i>

14:53.392 --> 14:54.977
<i>Maybe in its current state...</i>

15:12.411 --> 15:14.330
Hmm, how interesting!

15:14.413 --> 15:15.956
Just how many are there?

15:18.208 --> 15:19.793
They mimic muscle movements

15:19.877 --> 15:22.671
by expanding
and contracting at the joints.

15:23.172 --> 15:24.757
I wonder if they're hermaphrodites.

15:25.591 --> 15:27.801
I wonder which creature laid the egg.

15:29.428 --> 15:31.847
I forgot I don't have time
for this right now!

15:33.015 --> 15:34.350
Excuse me!

15:34.433 --> 15:37.227
You...! Just let go!

15:37.311 --> 15:39.355
Everyone! Come over here now!

15:39.438 --> 15:40.731
- Now's not the time!
- Now's not the time!

15:45.778 --> 15:46.695
Huh?

15:52.117 --> 15:54.703
What was that? How did you do that?!

15:57.039 --> 15:58.582
So there was a magic-user?!

15:59.166 --> 16:00.751
There were no magic-users.

16:00.834 --> 16:03.837
The Living Armors weren't controlled.

16:03.921 --> 16:05.297
They were creatures.

16:05.881 --> 16:06.715
Huh?

16:06.799 --> 16:09.051
Look at the inside of this armor.

16:09.134 --> 16:11.553
There are two layers,
and something is clinging between them.

16:13.097 --> 16:14.723
This is the identity of the Living Armor.

16:18.435 --> 16:20.980
<i>By clasping hands inside the armor,</i>

16:21.063 --> 16:23.816
<i>they were acting
as muscles of different parts.</i>

16:25.317 --> 16:26.860
Even though each creature is weak,

16:26.944 --> 16:29.738
by dividing the body parts
and utilizing the armor's structure,

16:30.531 --> 16:32.491
they can imitate human movements.

16:33.492 --> 16:35.119
Unluckily for us,

16:35.202 --> 16:37.871
it seems we encountered them
during the spawning season this time.

16:37.955 --> 16:41.125
Spawning?! These things hatch from eggs?!

16:41.208 --> 16:44.378
That's right! They hatch from eggs!

16:44.461 --> 16:46.588
No one realized this until now!

16:46.672 --> 16:49.925
Everyone thought they were simply
Living Armor controlled by magic!

16:50.009 --> 16:53.303
If I were to reveal this fact,
it would cause a huge stir in our circle!

16:53.846 --> 16:56.890
You know how he talks fast

16:56.974 --> 16:58.142
when it comes to monsters?

16:58.225 --> 16:59.518
It creeps me out.

16:59.601 --> 17:01.395
Hush! Stop that.

17:01.478 --> 17:02.646
Senshi!

17:02.730 --> 17:05.899
We might not be able to eat armor,
but what about the stuff inside?

17:05.983 --> 17:08.318
Looks pretty nutritious, doesn't it?

17:11.780 --> 17:15.159
There's no way we can eat something
so mysterious!

17:15.242 --> 17:17.286
Now, now, Marcille.

17:17.369 --> 17:20.831
Every food is a mystery
until that first bite.

17:22.958 --> 17:24.710
Now's not the time to be trying it!

17:24.793 --> 17:25.961
Let's give it a shot.

17:27.379 --> 17:29.339
I'm using this ingredient
for the first time,

17:29.423 --> 17:30.841
so I'm not confident, though.

17:30.924 --> 17:32.468
Thanks, Senshi.

17:32.551 --> 17:33.927
No way!

17:34.428 --> 17:36.513
What if it's extremely poisonous?

17:37.097 --> 17:41.852
I doubt a creature with potent poison
would hide itself inside a shell.

17:42.936 --> 17:45.314
But how should I cook it?

17:45.814 --> 17:47.232
This underside...

17:47.316 --> 17:50.027
didn't budge when I tried
to pry it open with my hands.

17:50.611 --> 17:54.364
But when I cut this part with a blade,
it couldn't close the gap.

17:54.448 --> 17:57.701
Maybe it was an adductor muscle
that it uses to close the gap,

17:57.785 --> 17:59.536
like a scallop.

17:59.620 --> 18:01.872
I see. So it's a shellfish.

18:02.456 --> 18:03.874
All right, I've decided.

18:03.957 --> 18:06.543
Pry the meat from the armor, will you?

18:15.469 --> 18:16.553
It drowned.

18:16.637 --> 18:19.389
I guess you can't purge
the sand with water.

18:19.473 --> 18:22.893
I don't know if they even need
to be purged of sand.

18:23.477 --> 18:25.729
I'm a bit worried
about their internal organs,

18:25.813 --> 18:27.397
so I'll remove them.

18:27.481 --> 18:31.026
The sliced meat will go inside a soup.

18:31.110 --> 18:36.573
Oil, meat from the Living Armor,
herbs, and seasoning.

18:40.410 --> 18:41.328
And the head...

18:43.247 --> 18:44.414
will be steamed.

18:45.249 --> 18:48.168
And finally,
we might as well make the classic dish.

18:55.259 --> 18:56.260
It's ready!

18:58.262 --> 19:01.181
270
GRILLED LIVING ARMOR

19:01.265 --> 19:04.184
STEAM-BAKED LIVING ARMOR

19:04.977 --> 19:06.603
Marcille, which do you want to have first?

19:06.687 --> 19:07.604
What?

19:07.688 --> 19:09.606
I-I'll have the soup, then...

19:09.690 --> 19:13.610
Wait, do antidotes
work against food poisoning as well?

19:13.694 --> 19:15.696
It doesn't smell bad.

19:15.779 --> 19:18.240
It smells faintly of iron.

19:18.907 --> 19:19.950
Laios,

19:20.033 --> 19:20.868
here.

19:21.368 --> 19:22.828
It's hot!

19:27.416 --> 19:29.293
Why are you all looking at me like that?

19:30.294 --> 19:33.297
You've been craving Living Armor
for a long time now, right?

19:33.380 --> 19:35.966
We shouldn't eat it before you do.

19:36.049 --> 19:37.593
I see...

19:37.676 --> 19:39.595
If he dies, let's leave him here.

19:39.678 --> 19:40.721
Yeah.

19:46.351 --> 19:47.269
- <i>Did he die?</i>
- <i>Did he die?</i>

19:47.352 --> 19:48.812
It's delicious!

19:49.313 --> 19:52.357
What on earth? It's so delicious!

19:52.441 --> 19:56.403
At first, it tasted bland,
but the flavor kicks in later!

19:56.486 --> 19:59.281
How long does it take before you
start having symptoms of food poisoning?

19:59.364 --> 20:00.657
It depends on the food.

20:05.370 --> 20:06.747
So that's what it tastes like.

20:06.830 --> 20:10.000
Not bad, but I think
I could've cooked it better.

20:10.083 --> 20:11.376
How about the dish you have?

20:14.338 --> 20:17.674
Well, I suppose this one should be safe
because it was stir-fried with herbs.

20:22.095 --> 20:23.388
H-How is it?

20:24.223 --> 20:25.557
It's not bad.

20:38.111 --> 20:39.821
What do you think, Marcille?

20:39.905 --> 20:43.242
It tastes a bit like mushrooms.

20:43.325 --> 20:44.284
Right?

20:45.577 --> 20:47.663
The steam-baked one
looks ready and tasty, too.

20:47.746 --> 20:50.415
It has to taste great!

20:53.502 --> 20:55.045
It tastes like mold.

20:55.128 --> 20:57.756
The odor of the helmet
must've gotten trapped in it.

21:01.260 --> 21:02.427
Here.

21:03.303 --> 21:06.473
You know, I've been in the dungeon
for a long time now,

21:06.556 --> 21:09.101
but I never thought they were edible.

21:09.685 --> 21:13.230
Nobody would expect Living Armor
to be a sort of shellfish

21:13.313 --> 21:15.440
that hatch from eggs.

21:16.024 --> 21:19.111
Maybe when they're newborns
and juveniles, they're very small,

21:19.194 --> 21:21.697
and no one suspects them
to be Living Armor.

21:22.281 --> 21:24.700
<i>They probably form shells as they grow.</i>

21:24.783 --> 21:26.201
<i>Then, they start forming colonies.</i>

21:26.285 --> 21:29.830
<i>And when they can move,
they travel looking for other colonies.</i>

21:30.497 --> 21:33.834
<i>Maybe the armor standing in rows
were looking for partners.</i>

21:33.917 --> 21:38.672
<i>They are likely hermaphrodites
and the biggest colony lays an egg.</i>

21:39.172 --> 21:41.842
<i>Oh! That means...</i>

21:41.925 --> 21:43.635
The armor I occasionally see holding hands

21:43.719 --> 21:45.512
might not have been
adventurers fooling around.

21:45.595 --> 21:47.431
Maybe they were actually mating!

21:47.514 --> 21:48.849
You can drop it now.

21:50.100 --> 21:52.477
<i>To think the thing
I was so scared of for a time</i>

21:53.312 --> 21:56.231
<i>was such a tasty and feeble monster.</i>

21:57.941 --> 21:59.609
Your sword broke, huh?

22:00.444 --> 22:01.987
Why don't you take that one?

22:06.199 --> 22:07.075
Laios!

22:07.784 --> 22:11.163
If you're going to use that sword,
shall I test it to see if it's not cursed?

22:11.246 --> 22:12.831
No need!

22:12.914 --> 22:14.416
I'm absolutely sure it's not cursed!

22:14.499 --> 22:15.709
I can tell!

22:15.792 --> 22:17.294
You seem awfully confident.

22:18.253 --> 22:20.422
Don't come to me if you end up
with some weird curse.

22:23.508 --> 22:24.718
Everyone, wait for me!

22:26.261 --> 22:28.263
<i>Armed with a new sword,</i>

22:28.930 --> 22:30.640
<i>their journey continues.</i>

22:32.267 --> 22:35.854
<i>The other three had no way of knowing</i>

22:35.937 --> 22:38.815
<i>that they had a new companion.</i>

24:07.821 --> 24:11.992
Subtitle translation by: Ai Matsuoka
